        <PackageReleaseNotes>#### Added
- Stdin piping guide; stdin contract tests and derivation property tests.

#### Changed
- All six `ProcessConfiguration` derivation sites (shell middleware, `ShellRewriter` branches) now build through the internal `ProcessConfigurationDerivation.Derive` hook; `WithValidationRules`/`WithMaxBufferedOutputBytes` share one copy routine. No public API change.
- `RetryConditions.ExitCodeZero()` renamed to `NonZeroExitCode()` (the old name meant the opposite); update pre-release call sites.
- ADR-0001 updated; no new IVT grant.

## Fixed
- `StartAsync(CancellationToken)` returns at launch again instead of waiting for exit; call `WaitForExitOrTimeoutAsync`/`CaptureBufferedResultAsync` explicitly. Raw-mode timeouts fire mid-run again.
- `IExternalProcess.StartAsync(config, ct)` honors `RedirectStandardInput`; a configured stdin writer with redirection disabled is a no-op everywhere.
- Graceful cancellation is deterministic: `CancellationThrowsException` is honoured when set and never when false; interrupt faults are observed; `ProcessTimeoutPolicy.Enabled = false` really disables timeouts; no more token leakage.
- `MiddlewareContext.Next` no longer re-runs the current middleware; sub-chains no longer leak the outer context; `ProcessMiddlewareBuilder.Build()` preserves registration order.
- `UseDefaultShell()` uses the safe PowerShell switch set (`-NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command`).
- `WithMaxBufferedOutputBytes(config, null)` clears the cap (unbounded) instead of inheriting it.
- Empty-string environment variable values are allowed (clearing a variable); keys stay non-empty.
- `AddCliInvoke` resolves `IProcessConfigurationBuilder` as a blank-builder factory instead of throwing.
- XML doc corrections.</PackageReleaseNotes>
